speechtext:
Madam Speaker, 1 have a question for the Minister of National Revenue. Last week representations were made to the Minister by all Members of the House, and I believe a question was directed to him by the Hon. Member for Brampton-Georgetown about the "Custer's Last Revenge" cassettes. The Minister undertook to study this and to give us a reply. Has he had an opportunity to do this?
December 1, 1982

[Translation}
